{{!-- add-chantry-inventory-effects-and-roster (task 3.5) — the Integrated Effects tab.

      `traits['integrated-effects'] ●●●` used to say there were fifteen points of Effects and not
      say WHICH. This tab is the which, plus every figure the book makes checkable.

      TWO POOLS, AND CONFUSING THEM WOULD BE THE EASY MISTAKE (design.md D2). The CONSTRUCTION pool
      (`system.pool`, on the Rasgos tab) pays for the circles of this Trait at 2 points each. Each
      circle then grants its own EFFECT pool, and that one is not linear: 4, 8, 15, 20, 25, 35, 45,
      55, 70, 90 for 1…10 circles, straight out of `m20-the-operative-dossier`'s own table. It is
      held as a TABLE in `module/scripts/chantry-effects.js` and never interpolated; above ten
      circles the sheet says the pool is off the table rather than inventing one.

      EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS DERIVED, none is stored. `evaluateEffects()` computes the cost of each
      effect (the sum of its Sphere levels — "un efecto de Mente 2 … costaría 2 puntos", "Fuerzas 3
      / Cardinal 2 / Vida 1 / Materia 1 / Tiempo 4 … costaría 11"), the total spent, the remainder,
      the weekly Quintessence upkeep (one per effect) against the Node, and which Spheres exceed the
      cap. A stored `cost` on the data is discarded on read, so the two can never drift.

      THE THREE RULES THIS TAB SURFACES, and the difference between them matters:
        * a Sphere level above the Chantry's own rating is ILLEGAL — the Chantry's rating IS the
          Areté these effects cast with — so the row and the offending Sphere are both marked;
        * spending more than the pool is ILLEGAL, so the total is marked;
        * Zona de Realidad 0 makes the effects VULGAR, not illegal. That is a notice, never a block:
          the book conditions coincidence, not existence.
      Nothing here refuses to render because of any of the three. A sheet that hides a GM's own data
      because it disagrees with it is worse than one that shows it and says so.

      NOTHING IS SPENT AUTOMATICALLY. The upkeep is shown and compared against Nodo; no
      Quintessence is deducted anywhere (proposal.md "Qué NO").

      CONTEXT DEPTH — the trap this system has already shipped twice. Inside `{{#each integrated.rows}}`
      a bare `locked` resolves against the ROW, not the sheet, so `(eq locked false)` would be false
      forever and the delete control would never render, not even unlocked. It is `../locked` one
      loop deep and `../../locked` inside the Sphere loop, and those depths were established by
      PROBING THE RENDERED HTML (`.github/scripts/test-chantry-sheet-render.mjs` renders this part in
      both lock states and counts write controls), not by counting braces. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}">

	<div class="chantry-body flexcol {{#if locked}}locked{{/if}}">

		<div class="clearareaBox area-box chantry-effects-summary">

			<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont">
				<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.headline"}}</span>
			</div>

			<div class="clearareaBox row">
				<div class="pullLeft headlineNormal ability-headlineWidth">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.pool"}}</div>
				<div class="pullLeft chantry-effects-figures">
					{{#if integrated.pooloverflow}}
						{{!-- Above the ten circles the Dossier tabulates. Said out loud rather than
						      extrapolated — see this file's header and design.md D2. --}}
						<span class="item-warning">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.pooloverflow"}}</span>
					{{else}}
						<span class="chantry-effects-pool">{{integrated.pool}}</span>
						&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;
						{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.spent"}}:
						<span class="chantry-effects-spent {{#if integrated.overspent}}item-warning{{/if}}">{{integrated.spent}}</span>
						&nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp;
						{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.remaining"}}:
						<span class="chantry-effects-remaining {{#if integrated.overspent}}item-warning{{/if}}">{{integrated.remaining}}</span>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="clearareaBox row">
				<div class="pullLeft headlineNormal ability-headlineWidth">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.spherecap"}}</div>
				<div class="pullLeft chantry-effects-figures">{{integrated.spherecap}}</div>
			</div>

			<div class="clearareaBox row">
				<div class="pullLeft headlineNormal ability-headlineWidth">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.upkeep"}}</div>
				<div class="pullLeft chantry-effects-figures">
					<span class="chantry-effects-upkeep {{#if integrated.upkeepshortfall}}item-warning{{/if}}">{{integrated.upkeep}}</span>
					&nbsp;/&nbsp;
					{{localize "wod.chantry.traits.node"}}: <span class="chantry-effects-node">{{integrated.node}}</span>
					{{#if integrated.upkeepshortfall}}
						<span class="item-warning chantry-effects-shortfall" title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.shortfall'}}">
							<i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
							{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.shortfall"}}
						</span>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>

			{{#if integrated.vulgar}}
				<div class="clearareaBox row chantry-effects-vulgar">
					<div class="pullLeft item-warning" title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.vulgar'}}">
						<i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.vulgar"}}
					</div>
				</div>
			{{/if}}

		</div>

		<div class="clearareaBox area-box chantry-effects-list">

			<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont">
				<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.list"}}</span>

				{{#if (eq locked false)}}
					<button type="button" class="v3-iconbtn chantry-effect-add" data-action="effectCreate"
							title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.add'}}">
						<i class="icon fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						<span class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.add"}}</span>
					</button>
				{{/if}}
			</div>

			{{#if integrated.rows}}
				{{#each integrated.rows as |row|}}
					<div class="chantry-effect-row {{#if row.overcap}}chantry-effect-overcap{{/if}}" data-index="{{row.index}}">

						<div class="chantry-effect-head">
							{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
								<input class="inputdata editable chantry-effect-name" type="text" value="{{row.name}}"
										data-source="effect" data-field="name" data-index="{{row.index}}"
										placeholder="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.name'}}" autocomplete="off" />
							{{else}}
								<span class="chantry-effect-name">{{row.name}}</span>
							{{/if}}

							<span class="chantry-effect-cost {{#if row.overcap}}item-warning{{/if}}"
									title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.cost'}}">{{row.cost}}</span>

							{{#if row.overcap}}
								<span class="item-warning chantry-effect-overcap-flag" title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.overcap'}}">
									<i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
								</span>
							{{/if}}

							{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
								<button type="button" class="v3-iconbtn chantry-effect-spheread" data-action="effectSphereAdd"
										data-index="{{row.index}}" title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.addsphere'}}">
									<i class="icon fa-solid fa-circle-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
									<span class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.addsphere"}}</span>
								</button>
								<a class="pointer item-delete chantry-effect-delete" data-action="effectDelete"
										data-index="{{row.index}}" title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.remove'}}"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
							{{/if}}
						</div>

						<div class="chantry-effect-spheres">
							{{#each row.spheres as |sphere sphereindex|}}
								<span class="chantry-effect-sphere {{#if sphere.overcap}}item-warning{{/if}}">
									{{#if (eq ../../locked false)}}
										{{!-- The option list is BUILT IN JS (`sphere.options`, each entry
										      carrying its own `selected`) rather than iterated out of
										      CONFIG here. Two reasons, both learned the hard way in this
										      file: iterating a config list from inside two nested
										      `{{#each}}`es needs a `../../../` that nobody can verify by
										      reading, and comparing the option against the current value
										      needs another. Neither depth exists any more. --}}
										<select class="inputdata editable chantry-effect-sphere-key"
												data-source="effectsphere" data-field="sphere"
												data-index="{{sphere.index}}" data-sphereindex="{{sphereindex}}">
											{{#each sphere.options as |option|}}
												<option value="{{option.key}}" {{#if option.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{localize option.labelkey}}</option>
											{{/each}}
										</select>
										<input class="inputdata editable chantry-effect-sphere-level" type="number" min="0" max="10"
												value="{{sphere.level}}"
												data-source="effectsphere" data-field="level"
												data-index="{{sphere.index}}" data-sphereindex="{{sphereindex}}" />
										<a class="pointer item-delete chantry-effect-sphere-delete" data-action="effectSphereDelete"
												data-index="{{sphere.index}}" data-sphereindex="{{sphereindex}}"
												title="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.removesphere'}}"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-circle-minus" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
									{{else}}
										{{localize sphere.labelkey}} {{sphere.level}}
									{{/if}}
								</span>
							{{/each}}
						</div>

						<div class="chantry-effect-description">
							{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
								<input class="inputdata editable" type="text" value="{{row.description}}"
										data-source="effect" data-field="description" data-index="{{row.index}}"
										placeholder="{{localize 'wod.chantry.effects.description'}}" autocomplete="off" />
							{{else}}
								{{row.description}}
							{{/if}}
						</div>

					</div>
				{{/each}}
			{{else}}
				<p class="v3-empty">{{localize "wod.chantry.effects.empty"}}</p>
			{{/if}}

		</div>

	</div>

</section>
